      <memberdef kind="property" id="classQAccelPlot_1_1TextLabel_1a49cdcedafbfa499cce14f885eb62e920" prot="public" static="no" readable="yes" writable="no" gettable="no" privategettable="no" protectedgettable="no" settable="no" privatesettable="no" protectedsettable="no">
        <type>QString</type>
        <definition>QString QAccelPlot::TextLabel::unitText</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>unitText</name>
        <qualifiedname>QAccelPlot::TextLabel::unitText</qualifiedname>
        <read>unitText</read>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Prefixed unit the tick label formatter chose for the current ticks, such as &quot;mm&quot;. Read-only. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The owning <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1Axis" kindref="compound">Axis</ref> or <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1ColorBar" kindref="compound">ColorBar</ref> updates it whenever it computes its ticks. It is empty when the formatter shows no unit, as with every built-in formatter except <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1UnitTickLabelFormatter" kindref="compound">UnitTickLabelFormatter</ref></computeroutput>. While it is set, the owner paints its axis label with <computeroutput>unitFormat</computeroutput>, such as &quot;Distance (mm)&quot;. An <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1Axis" kindref="compound">Axis</ref> <computeroutput>delegate</computeroutput> can bind to it. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="QAccelPlot/src/QAccelPlot/axis/TextLabel.hpp" line="37" column="5" bodyfile="QAccelPlot/src/QAccelPlot/axis/TextLabel.hpp" bodystart="37" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="property" id="classQAccelPlot_1_1TextLabel_1a1d937994093f06c5a32d79909d4361a0" prot="public" static="no" readable="yes" writable="yes" gettable="no" privategettable="no" protectedgettable="no" settable="no" privatesettable="no" protectedsettable="no">
        <type>QString</type>
        <definition>QString QAccelPlot::TextLabel::unitFormat</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>unitFormat</name>
        <qualifiedname>QAccelPlot::TextLabel::unitFormat</qualifiedname>
        <read>unitFormat</read>
        <write>setUnitFormat</write>
        <briefdescription>
<para>How the painted axis label combines <computeroutput>text</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>%1</computeroutput>) and <computeroutput>unitText</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>%2</computeroutput>). Default: &quot;%1 (%2)&quot;. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>For example, &quot;%1 [%2]&quot; paints &quot;Distance [mm]&quot; and &quot;%1 / %2&quot; paints &quot;Distance / mm&quot;. It applies only while both <computeroutput>text</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>unitText</computeroutput> are set: an empty <computeroutput>text</computeroutput> paints <computeroutput>unitText</computeroutput> alone, and an empty <computeroutput>unitText</computeroutput> paints <computeroutput>text</computeroutput> alone. Assign <computeroutput>undefined</computeroutput> to return to the default. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="QAccelPlot/src/QAccelPlot/axis/TextLabel.hpp" line="43" column="5" bodyfile="QAccelPlot/src/QAccelPlot/axis/TextLabel.hpp" bodystart="43" bodyend="-1"/>
